  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieved 0.591 acc, a substantial +10.6% gain over config_001 (singleprofile, 0.485), confirming that multiprofile aggregation is the most impactful design choice so far. Image-only is weak (0.208), so RNA-centric exploration is the priority. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether transformer aggregation (which models inter-profile interactions) outperforms simple average pooling. This experiment (config_003) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding encoder (pca_n2000), profile setting (multiprofile), and modality (rna_only) fixed, giving a clean single-variable comparison against config_002. Why this is the best next step: With 6 experiments remaining, isolating the aggregation effect is the highest-information experiment because the result directly determines whether to invest remaining budget in transformer-based multimodal configs (configs 020/021/026/027 etc.) or to focus on encoder upgrades (scvi, scgpt) with avgpool. It is a low-risk, high-information exploitation of the current best direction."
}

